{"Allowing negative start_offset for previous cursors is incompatible with Django QuerySet slicing - when cursor.is_prev is true, this can generate slices like queryset[-10:20] which Django QuerySets don't support and will raise an error": 0.885871171951294, "Accessing organization_context.member.has_global_access without guarding against a missing member can raise AttributeError for non-members when organization_context.member is None": 0.6529754400253296, "The trimming condition still uses offset instead of start_offset, which can desynchronize the overfetch logic - when offset != start_offset (e.g., after clamping), the condition len(results) == offset + limit + extra no longer matches the fetched range and can trim the extra record incorrectly": 0.8093786835670471, "The offset/extra trimming logic for cursor.is_prev assumes non-negative offsets, so when negative offsets are allowed this may produce incorrect slice boundaries or result removal": 0.8429290056228638, "The OptimizedCursorPaginator largely duplicates the existing BasePaginator.get_result flow with minor conditional changes, creating maintenance risk - should extract shared logic into reusable helpers or parameterize the existing paginator": 0.2805665135383606}